WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.939
I don't make things for museums

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.289
or for art collectors.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.429
And if you think that what I'm

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.899
saying is bullshit, immediately

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.159
change the channel and do something

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.160
else.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.569
Do you want to build a rocket ship

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.429
but don't have the deep pockets

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.499
of Jeff Bezos, Elon Musk

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.449
or Richard Branson?

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.039
You might want to turn to the Rocket

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.049
Factory, a trans dimensional

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.879
manufacturing plant created by

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.919
artist Tom Sachs, in which

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.079
you can build and own a personalized

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.939
rocket in both the physical and

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.409
virtual world.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.699
The project is one of the most

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.979
inventive uses of NFTs,

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.839
a groundbreaking technology that

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.389
makes digital items one of a kind.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.339
By giving them a unique code that

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.339
can't be duplicated or forged.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.749
The rocket factory builds on

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.879
previous themes in sex work,

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.919
such as creating painstakingly

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.839
realistic reproductions of familiar

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.729
objects and in a nod

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.739
to Andy Warhol referencing

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.019
popular brands and companies

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.939
long obsessed with spaceflight.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.439
He's also created three different

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.419
space program installations,

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.219
each of which contemplates what it

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.469
means to fly to the Moon, Mars

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.470
and beyond.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.099
Sachs' art makes use of the new

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.779
form of digital commons called the

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.579
blockchain, which is the shared

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.929
public database that makes it

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.819
possible to prove that you and

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.219
you alone own an NFT.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.379
Of the Metaverse, the 3D

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.239
virtual world where some believe

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.099
a great deal of human interaction

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.989
will soon be migrating and

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.909
of our persistent longing for a

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.319
new frontier.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.149
All of which are characteristics

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.219
of what is often called Web

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.109
3.0, the next

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.999
phase in the evolution of the

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.229
internet.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.789
Reason spoke with Sachs in his

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.559
Manhattan studio about the role of

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.969
psychedelics in his creative

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.889
process, how the internet has

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.869
radically flattened and improved

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.759
the relationship between artist and

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.549
audience, and why his meticulously

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.889
handcrafted NFT rockets

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.809
can be just as exciting,

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.759
innovative and inspiring

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.799
as the ones made by Bezos,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.269
Musk and Branson.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.689
Tom Sachs, thanks for talking to

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:08.690
Reason.

